WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.620
"Cong..."

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.080
"...grat..."

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.080
"...tula..."

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.080
"...tions"

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.750
"Congratulations" "As a charismatic
Let's Player, you have been chosen to participate
in a closed stage of <i>The Ones Within - Genome</i>."

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.290
"This privilege cannot be
transferred or retracted."

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.910
"Congratulations"

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.250
"We will come get you."

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.370
Whoa...

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.450
Are you serious?

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.540
Huh?

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.000
Um...

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.250
When you find someone collapsed...

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.290
One. Call out to them.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.040
"1) Call out to them"
Ma'am? Ma'am? Ma'am!

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.160
"2) Check for pulse and breathing"
Two. Check for pulse and breathing.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.250
Let me check your neck for a pulse...

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.500
Oh, thank goodne--

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.450
Wh-What are you, some pervert?!

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.950
Wh-Whoa, calm down...

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.160
My name's Akatsuki Iride.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.370
I'm not anyone shushpicious.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.950
You are in anyone's book!

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.040
Where in the world are we?

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.660
That's what I'd like to know, too.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.080
If you're a perverted mountain climber
that happens to be a big liar,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.450
this all makes perfect sense.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.330
Could you please stop with the speculation?

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:04.580
The thing is, I'm pretty sure
I've heard your voice before.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.370
I have full confidence in my memory.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:11.700
I never forget stuff once I take it in, but...

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.290
Anyway, let's hurry and
find a phone or the police.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.450
If we don't get off this mountain before
it gets dark and a bear shows up...

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.450
Huh?!

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.500
Wh-What the--?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.500
Shh! It hasn't found us yet.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.290
Let's wait it out here.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.620
If it finds us, we don't stand a chance.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.620
Achoo!

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.660
Idiot! Why couldn't you hold it in?!

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.040
Sorry! I'm not proud of it, but...

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.330
...I've got pretty much every
pollen allergy in Japan.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.000
You're right! You shouldn't be proud!

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.660
Wha--?!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.200
A-A rat?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.040
Greetings, you two.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.250
What are you standing around for?

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.450
You just need to smash their eyes.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.540
Huh?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.370
Go for their eyes. Smash or gouge them out.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.200
They're surprisingly easy to beat.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.450
I'll lend you this.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.620
I-I'm not cut out for this!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.660
The boy can do his best unarmed...

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.410
Why the hell did you try
running off by yourself?!

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.120
I-It's all a misunderstanding!

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.450
Hello there.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.660
Your face sure is huge!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.700
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.870
Pardon me while I feel your paws!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.290
Seriously, what are you doing?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.700
I've always wanted to touch a panda!

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:38.700
And his paw is oh so soothing!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.330
Don't be soothed!

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.830
Y-You idiot!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.410
Do you have allergies, too?

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.290
There's nothing to be afraid of!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.080
Did you see his eyes when we were running?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.700
They weren't looking down towards us at all.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:18.000
He's probably just on a walk or something.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.200
He was never after us from the start.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.750
Isn't that right?

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.700
Pandarou?

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:35.750
It's impressive how you noticed
in that sort of situation.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.540
Excellent. Splendid.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.910
To think you'd clear
the first game so quickly...

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.500
Nice to meet you. I supervise 13th Avenue
of<i> The Ones Within - Genome</i>.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.330
My name is Paka.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.830
Stage 1 was "Animal Battle."

00:05:53.830 --> 00:06:00.540
To clear it, you must defeat the
gigantic creatures coming for you, but...

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:05.290
What a surprise from the escape
game Let's Player, Mr. Iride.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.250
I've never seen anyone
befriend the panda before.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.620
How very intriguing.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:18.580
New play styles can draw in and
fascinate the hearts of viewers...

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:22.200
...resulting in a tremendous
surge of total views.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:25.250
I'm expecting great things from you.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:29.580
Please, everyone.
Take a look at your left wrist.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.370
Huh?

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.040
Ew, what's this?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.160
It won't come off.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.500
That's an epidermal counter.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.700
We embedded you with nanochips
while you were asleep.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.790
It's linked with the main server in the tower...

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:51.080
...and displays the view count in real time.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.750
View count, did you say?

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:57.200
Indeed. Is the term not
one you're familiar with?

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.250
That includes you two as well.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.080
Sengoku Let's Player, Mr. Onigasaki.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.450
Horror Let's Player, Ms. Sarayashiki.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:08.250
Hey... I never told you my name.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.620
Who are you?

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:11.450
Take that off and show your face.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.580
No thank you! It's too embarrassing!

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.950
All you 13th Avenue people are so impatient.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:24.620
Let me get straight to the point.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:28.540
There is only one thing you must
accomplish while you're here:

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.540
To make that counter reach
100,000,000... In other words,

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:35.250
you must reach 100,000,000 views...

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:39.790
...during this live stream of
<i>The Ones Within - Genome</i>.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:44.370
Furthermore, your play time is infinite.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:48.830
I urge you to play as if
your life depends on it.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.870
"The Ones Within"

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.450
"Day Duty" "Akatsuki Iride"
"Karin Sarayashiki" "Nei"

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:24.750
"Day Duty" "Akatsuki Iride"
"Karin Sarayashiki" "Nei"
Now then...

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.790
Let's introduce the comrades you'll
experience pain and pleasure with.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.080
Puffy, puffy.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:36.370
Starting at the window, say your name
and game specialty in a lively voice.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.830
Okay! Nice to meet you! I'm Akatsuki Iride!

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.040
I specialize in escape games!

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:45.410
I like nature, vacations, and paws of all types!

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.040
You're too happy!

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.660
S-Sensei said to be lively...

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.790
Have you no sense of danger?

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.120
Don't forget he abducted all of us!

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.000
The next seat please.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.620
I-I'm Himiko Inaba.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.660
I like nurturing games.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:06.330
I'm actually very passionate about
watching your soft-spoken streams.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:10.790
It's such an honor as a fan
to hear your voice in person.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.870
Do you think you could possibly
whisper something to me?

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:18.500
"I love Mr. Paka," into my ear?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.700
It's not your turn yet, Mr. Kudou.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.370
Screw these introductions.
Let us go free already.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:36.250
Mr. Kudou, I told you that violence
towards me is against the rules.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.040
You'll be punished if this keeps up.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:43.330
Go ahead then. Try me.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:48.410
Be very careful eating
your meals starting tonight.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.080
I'm putting lots of peppers in them.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.700
That's nothing!

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.040
Um, that was Anya Kudou.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.870
He's a Let's Player specializing
in fighting games.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.120
Next up is me.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.120
Yuzu Roromori. Puzzle games, mazes,
and speed runs are my thing.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:11.250
My hobby is researching tropical plants.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.370
Yuzu?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:16.500
Are you Yuzu from
Rororo's Speedrun Channel?

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.410
I'm Akki from the Hay Fever Channel.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:22.000
Oh, Akki!

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.870
Oh, wow. You were abducted, too?

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.160
You know her?

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:27.040
Yup!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.620
"Bury myself in leaves at a park stream"
We got along last year during a
"Bury myself in leaves at a park stream."

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.750
"Bury myself in leaves at a park stream"
Okay, I've heard enough.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:37.950
I'm Karen Sarayashiki.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.290
I do horror Let's Plays.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.750
Got a problem with that?

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.000
Ms. Sarayashiki is such a cool one.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:49.000
That's the "#1 girl streamer people
want to get stepped on by" for you.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.540
When you play, you're so--

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.830
Shut it or you'll be a fur coat.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:54.870
Next row, please.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:58.330
Zakuro Oshigiri. I play stealth games.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.450
Can we get this dumb stunt over with?

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.700
That depends on how hard you all work.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:09.370
I already know we're all streamers
that Let's Played <i>The Ones Within</i>.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:13.700
But why did you choose us?
What comes after 100,000,000 views?

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:15.950
What's your true objective?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.370
Neigh...

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.040
Neigh?

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:22.450
Neigh!

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:26.700
Not going to spill your secrets easily, huh?

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.580
Uh, Zak... I think he's just
screwing with you, meow!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.750
I'm Kaikoku Onigasaki.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:36.040
I mostly do Sengoku
and Japanese-style games.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.370
Nice to meet you.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:40.500
Thank you, Mr. Onigasaki.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:45.000
Last but not least, Mr. Aikawa.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:50.750
Hmm?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.120
Mr. Aikawa!

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.410
A-All right, then...

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.910
"Personal History" "Makino Aikawa"
"Feb 14, 1998"
He's Makino Aikawa...

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:08.290
"Personal History" "Makino Aikawa"
"Feb 14, 1998"
...a dating sim player who uses his eyes
to conquer rather than words.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:11.040
However, like his streams of very few words,

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:15.120
it's exceedingly rare
for him to speak at length.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.160
That ain't no stream!

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.500
In any case, everyone has
now been introduced.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:23.580
We will begin the election for Stage 2.

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:26.410
Huh? Wait. You haven't explained...

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.450
Paka. Paka.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:32.620
"Stage 2"
Stage 2. "Ouija Exchange."
Four players needed.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:33.040
"Stage 2"
These straws you'll be drawing
I stayed up late to make.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.620
These straws you'll be drawing
I stayed up late to make.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.580
The people who draw the Paka straws--

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.790
Screw you! How about you shove those--

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.700
Oh? Do you wish to retire?

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.200
In that case, you'd be disqualified...

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:54.290
...and imprisoned in the "White Room"
on the lowest floor of Genome Tower.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:58.910
Alone you would stay until
the others reach 100,000,000 views.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:03.040
In that secret, cramped room,
you'll wait for eternity.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:09.580
This is someone from the past who
complained too much, just like you.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:13.500
All while never knowing
that his friends had failed,

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:19.450
he waited for their arrival,
on and on and on...

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.290
Oh?

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:30.500
Don't you think that was a bit in poor taste?

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:33.200
One bit of advice...

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:38.910
You all would do well to understand
the situation you're currently in.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:45.290
Injury and death are real possibilities
because this is a real Let's Play.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:50.620
In the real world, do you think
there are resets and save points?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:57.620
Now then, let us get back to
deciding the players for Stage 2.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.830
Mr. Paka?

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.290
Are we allowed to volunteer?

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:10.290
Hey...

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.290
You're totally an idiot, aren't you?

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.700
Naw, he's a moron.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.750
I can't help my curiosity.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:18.580
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
Akatsuki Iridiot.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.500
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
Name change: White-hair wacko.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.080
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
It looks like we're together again, Karin.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.580
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
Would you shut it? I've got the worst of luck.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:29.250
In any case, we've got no choice now.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:30.620
That's right.

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:34.830
"Yes"             "No"

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.000
Hey, what are you doing?

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.790
You think I'm doing that? You're all idiots.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.500
I ain't listening to that jerk.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:52.620
Who the hell plays Ouija?
I'm not some grade-schooler brat.

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:55.620
That's exactly how a brat would act.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.000
Eh?

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.450
Are you that against it?

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:01.410
Mmm?

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:06.080
All you've got to do is touch it with
the tip of your finger. Pretty please?

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.290
Hell no.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:11.120
What about if I eat all those
peppers you're getting?

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.620
It's moving on its own! Awesome!

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.000
H-How does this even work?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.910
Hey, which one of you is pushing it?

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:28.290
Be quiet. The spirit is saying their wish.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.450
"Wa."

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:30.870
"Ter."

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:31.950
"Please."

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.620
Water?

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.040
I think there was a tap in the hallway.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.870
Don't! You can't remove your finger!

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:44.370
If we don't do it in the right order,
the spirit won't leave and it'll possess you!

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.080
Oh...

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.830
Um, could we just use the vase?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.580
"Yes."

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:56.330
I think we got it.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.330
W-Wow. This is easier than I thought.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.700
It's moving again.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.250
"Yes"             "No"

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.330
"Friend."

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.040
This suddenly turned into life counseling.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.290
They don't have any friends?

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:14.870
Friends aren't something
you get. They're made.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:17.370
What's this guy think he's saying?

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.700
Would you two cut it out?

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.450
--Shuddap.
--Get a grip. You're unbelievable.

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:28.160
--In that case, do you want
to be friends with me?
--Get a grip. You're unbelievable.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:30.200
My name's Akatsuki Iride.

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.330
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.290
"Yes"                       "No"

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.500
It said okay!

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.000
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
Dummy! You're a moron!

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.580
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
Dumoron!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.410
Only one more.

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:51.120
"Yes"           "No"

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.200
"A."

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:55.000
"Ka."

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:56.370
"Tsu."

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.450
"Ki."

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:04.040
What are we supposed to do now?

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:10.830
Wait... What are you doing?

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:14.910
U-Um, I'm being pulled by something...

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.580
--It's doing it on its own! Wh-Whoa!

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.870
--What do we do now?
--It's doing it on its own! Wh-Whoa!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.950
Hey, occult girl!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.540
Tsk. You're useless.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.700
Listen here! Not everyone who
likes horror is good with ghosts!

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.660
Some people like horror but
not when it happens to them!

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:36.790
I'm perfectly fine though!

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.620
R-Right.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:44.540
Hey... You know what floor we're on?

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:45.700
Akatsuki!

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:57.330
Behind you.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.830
Someone's there.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.580
Wh-What?! What's that?

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:18.580
Ghost! His ghost came back already!

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:21.660
Oh, sorry. I'm still alive.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.160
Whew, that was something!

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.580
My stomach hasn't dropped
like that in a while.

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:34.870
Go fall!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.120
What's wrong?

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:45.160
Um, there's someone behind you.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.370
The hell? How'd you get in here?

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.580
Are you...

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.120
...that spirit just now?

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:18.750
Well, who are you?

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.950
Do you mind telling me your name?

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:32.700
Thank you... for the water.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:34.540
You're welcome.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.580
Will you... be my friend?

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:42.580
Of course.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.700
I'm glad.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:48.000
Then... come with me.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.500
Let's burn up together.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.620
Won't you come...

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.830
...and die with me?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.500
See? You'll soon forget about me...

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:10.830
You liar.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.540
She's burning everything!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.660
Get away, Iride! Iride! Iride!

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:39.410
We can be friends.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:47.250
But I...

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:50.040
...can't go with you right now.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:56.370
I've never broke a promise that I've made.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.620
Once it's all over...

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:05.160
...I promise.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:27.330
Good morning, Kudou.

00:22:27.330 --> 00:22:30.200
That's gross. Call me Anya.

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:32.620
Himiko!

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:39.660
The rest of you were waiting in the theater?

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:43.120
Yeah. I'm glad you're all okay.

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:53.160
What? Quit your staring.

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:57.120
Don't you think it's strange?

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:59.330
To clear it so suddenly...

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:05.700
Don't you dare lose that.
I'm not doing that all over again.

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:09.080
Also, I probably should apologize.

00:23:10.250 --> 00:23:12.250
For what?

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:14.790
For smacking you when we first met.

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:16.790
Oh, it's fine.

00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:18.040
You're not mad?

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.450
Not at all.

00:23:19.450 --> 00:23:20.830
Why not?

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:30.370
Actually, I don't get upset by most things.

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:34.250
Are you serious?

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:37.750
I knew it... You're weird after all.
